WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:04.640
Winter has come, and it's sent an avalanche
down on the HBO production offices.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:09.940
In May of 2017, as Game of Thrones neared
its seventh and penultimate season on HBO,

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:13.809
the network announced that it was exploring
the idea of expanding the world of dragons,

00:00:13.809 --> 00:00:17.620
White Walkers, and dudes whose maybe-girlfriends
are actually their aunts through multiple

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:18.620
spin-off series.

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:23.740
HBO set up five of these projects, all prequels
rather than straight-up spin-offs, according

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:25.700
to Thrones author George R.R.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:29.760
Martin, and recently handed a pilot order
to one being run by Kingsman and Kick-Ass

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:31.500
writer Jane Goldman.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.609
Franchise fans rejoiced at the news that at
least one of the spin-off series was in works.

00:00:35.609 --> 00:00:38.440
But now their merriment and revels must come
to an end.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:42.800
HBO president Casey Bloys had announced that
Goldman's project is the only Game of Thrones

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.100
spin-off moving forward at HBO.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:48.899
The four others are as good as dead, sitting
dormant for the time being.

00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:54.030
Bloys dropped the bombshell during the Television
Critics Association on Wednesday, July 25th,

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:58.190
telling those in attendance, "There are no
plans to make any others at this point."

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:03.190
According to Bloys, it was HBO's intention
from the start to brainstorm a bevy of projects

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:07.650
and then lock in just one series, allowing
creatives and executives to pour their passion

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:11.840
into a single project rather than split their
energy amongst various productions.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:16.970
Bloys explained: "The reason we did multiple
scripts, in the development process, [is because

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:20.160
we knew] out of five we'd be lucky to get
one we're excited about."

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.300
At least for now, fans will simply have to
be satisfied with watching Goldman's series,

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:28.950
said to follow Westeros' descent from the
Golden Age of Heroes into a dark era that

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:33.300
will alter everything we know about the fictional
world's history, House Stark, and "the mysteries

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.300
of the east."

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.310
Will that be enough to quench their Thrones
thirst?

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:40.530
We don't know yet, but we do know some more
details about Goldman's prequel series.

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:44.910
After the Television Critics Association summer
session on Wednesday, Bloys sat down with

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:47.250
Deadline to discuss the prequel in more detail.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:51.400
He revealed that the project will feature
an ensemble cast and highlight strong female

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:52.400
characters.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:56.190
He also noted that, despite what some may
assume with a female showrunner like Goldman

00:01:56.190 --> 00:02:00.730
on board, the prequel that centers on Westeros'
fall from the Golden Age of Heroes won't have

00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:04.740
a female lead in the same way that Game of
Thrones has a male lead in Kit Harington's

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:05.860
Jon Snow.

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:10.129
Bloys explained: "There are very strong female
characters but it's an ensemble, there [are]

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:12.359
men and women [...] Jane is a very good writer.

00:02:12.359 --> 00:02:15.150
We don't want to limit her to writing female
leads.

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:17.780
There are a lot of very complicated leads
in [the pilot]."

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:22.550
Game of Thrones is known for its complex female
characters, including Maisie Williams' sword-swinging

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:28.069
Arya Stark, Lena Headey's power-hungry Cersei
Lannister, and Gwendoline Christie's strong-yet-sweet

00:02:28.069 --> 00:02:32.090
Brienne of Tarth, but the show has also sparked
controversy for its portrayal of some of its

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:33.090
leading ladies.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:37.140
For years, viewers have criticized the way
showrunners David Benioff and D.B.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:41.599
Weiss have presented the series' women, calling
for the creatives to "stop punishing" them

00:02:41.599 --> 00:02:44.989
with public humiliation and physical and sexual
violence.

00:02:44.989 --> 00:02:49.180
Bloys touched on the fact that the untitled
spin-off won't overwork itself trying to tie

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:54.139
up any potential threads left loose by Game
of Thrones or answer all the questions fans

00:02:54.139 --> 00:02:55.420
of the series might have.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:59.549
Instead, it will make the most of being its
own entity, one that features all the same

00:02:59.549 --> 00:03:04.489
drama, tension, and shocks everyone loves
in Game of Thrones, while still standing separate

00:03:04.489 --> 00:03:06.110
from the original fantasy epic.

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:11.120
Bloys elaborated: "Jane did not go into that
wanting to answer anything about Game of Thrones;

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:12.950
it was the story that spoke to her.

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:17.099
[...] It will feel very different because
it's 8,000 years before, it's a very different

00:03:17.099 --> 00:03:19.510
setting, a very different time in Westeros.

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:21.900
It will feel different but still Game of Thrones."

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:25.719
Overall, this newness shouldn't scare you
off, diehard Game of Thrones fans.

00:03:25.719 --> 00:03:28.319
Goldman actually created the spin-off series
with George R.R.

00:03:28.319 --> 00:03:32.819
Martin based on a story the two developed
together, so you can rest assured that the

00:03:32.819 --> 00:03:34.440
prequel is in capable hands.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:38.590
How exactly those hands will shape the project,
we can't predict, but we're hoping the end

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:39.639
result is swell.

